{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"restful-chaseable-macaw","creation_channel":"cli","description":"# The `resolved_statuses` config keys have no reader after f020\n\nTask [rebar:f020-0960-2c42-4d61] deleted the dormant inbound absence-probe port, including\nthe shared classifier `classify_probe_response`. That classifier was the ONLY reader of the\noperator-facing resolved-status configuration. The keys and their plumbing survive and still\nvalidate, but nothing consults them.\n\n## What is orphaned\n\n* `jira.resolved_statuses` / `reconciler.resolved_statuses` — DOCUMENTED, validated config\n  keys (list of workflow state names).\n* `adapters/jira_datacenter/settings.py::DEFAULT_RESOLVED_STATUSES` and the\n  `JiraDataCenterSettings.resolved_statuses` field.\n* `JiraDataCenterTransport.__init__`'s `resolved_statuses` parameter and the\n  `self._resolved_statuses` attribute it stores — now write-only.\n\n## Why f020 deliberately did NOT remove them\n\nRemoving a DOCUMENTED, operator-facing config key is a user-visible surface change: an\nexisting `pyproject.toml` that sets `resolved_statuses` must not start hard-failing on\nupgrade without a decided deprecation path. That is its own deprecate-vs-remove decision,\nnot a rider on a behavior-neutral deletion. f020 left the keys with their current\nvalidation behavior so its own change stayed behavior-neutral.\n\n## The decision to make\n\nPick one, and record the reason:\n\n1. **Deprecate then remove** — keep accepting the keys for one release with a deprecation\n   warning naming the removal version, then delete key + plumbing.\n2. **Remove now** — treat a dead-but-accepted key as harmless-to-drop because it never\n   changed behavior in any shipped release where the port was already dormant.\n3. **Keep** — only if a concrete future reader is identified. Note that ADR 0028 rules\n   absence-vs-deletion discrimination OUTBOUND-owned, so the outbound path\n   (`outbound_differ._safe_get_issue` + `binding_walk`) is where any future consumer would\n   live; whether IT wants a workflow-name set is the real question behind this option.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] the decision is recorded on this ticket with its reason\n- [ ] the decision is executed: the keys are deprecated-with-warning, removed, or given a\n      named live reader\n- [ ] `docs/config.md` matches whatever was decided (no documented key without a reader,\n      and no removed key still documented)\n- [ ] the DC transport's `resolved_statuses` parameter / `_resolved_statuses` attribute is\n      either removed or genuinely read\n- [ ] `make lint`, `make typecheck` and `make test` are green\n- [ ] the change is `Verified +1` on Gerrit before the ticket is closed","id":"549c-032f-6cb0-4258","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Decide deprecate-vs-remove for the orphaned resolved_statuses config keys"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786519452830573001,"uuid":"7d132f4f-49bd-46eb-afea-82a603d2d8dc"}